        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: J. M. G. Le Clézio, Ogden Nash\n- Awards: Prix Renaudot, Nobel Prize in Literature\n- Works: Le Procès-Verbal, light verse\n- Topics: literary achievements, poetry\n\nFacts:\n- J. M. G. Le Clézio wrote over forty works.\n- In 1963, J. M. G. Le Clézio received the Prix Renaudot for his novel \"Le Procès-Veral\".\n- In 2008, J. M. G. Le Clézio received the Nobel Prize in Literature for his life's work and was cited as an \"author of new departures, poetic adventure and sensual ecstasy, explorer of a humanity beyond and below the reigning civilization\".\n- Ogden Nash was born on August 19, 1902, and died on May 19, 1971.\n- Ogden Nash was an American poet known for light verse.\n- Ogden Nash wrote over 500 pieces of light verse.",
